# Tribunal "Estate Sale": Geon Auline, a collector, names the Droth Dagger (10)
# and asks the player to get it from the widow Arnsa Thendas ("Yes, I'll help."
# is choice 1, journal 20). The player takes it from her locked chest in
# Thendas Manor; the dagger's own script logs 30 once the player holds it
# (DrothDagger). Handing it to Geon ("Here's the dagger." is choice 3) pays 800
# (70), and leaving his house logs 80 (DrothPost).
# Unlocking stands in for the lockpick. Ref FormIDs carry Tribunal.esm's slot 06.
# Run: python -m tools.live.test_instance mwtest --cases <this folder> --fast --checkpoints --stop-on-fail --load mwtest_ms_adulterer --timeout 2400
# See docs/commentary/headless_testing.md#quest-runs

case ms_estate_sale
run
player->PositionCell 68 300 -115 0 "Mournhold, Geon Auline's House"
until 600 "Geon Auline"->GetDistance player < 400
talk Geon Auline
ask collector
expect GetJournalIndex MS_EstateSale == 10
ask Droth Dagger
choose 1
expect GetJournalIndex MS_EstateSale == 20
bye
run
player->PositionCell 303 230 -106 0 "Mournhold, Thendas Manor"
until 300 GetPCCell "Mournhold, Thendas Manor" == 1
console 06AA37A4.unlock
activate 06AA37A4
close ContainerMenu
console 06AA37A4.removeallitems player
until 300 GetJournalIndex MS_EstateSale == 30
run
player->PositionCell 68 300 -115 0 "Mournhold, Geon Auline's House"
until 600 "Geon Auline"->GetDistance player < 400
talk Geon Auline
ask Droth Dagger
choose 3
expect GetJournalIndex MS_EstateSale == 70
expect player->GetItemCount "silver dagger_droth_unique" == 0
bye
run
player->PositionCell 303 230 -106 0 "Mournhold, Thendas Manor"
until 300 GetJournalIndex MS_EstateSale == 80
end
